Z||000010||87ECO5||03-10-2000||09:39 AM||||Ditto what MM said.  After seeing the stuff going on in the O/T section, I'd have to say it's a bad idea - even if we said "keep it Fiero-related only."  Some of us just like to instigate things and some of us don't know when to get up and walk away from the keyboard.  We'd end up fighting in real-time over which body style is better.<P>The O/T section was the proverbial snowball.  A chat room would be the very steep snow-covered hill.  I fear we would not see the forum celebrate its second anniversary.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mwbackus||03-10-2000||10:35 AM||||BM:  The firetalk thing is for a web enabled realtime chat system.  It has a bunch of features that include voice chat, forum chats, voicemail, and other stuff.  Its real easy to set up on any web page, just a few lines of html code, but requires a free client application similar to ICQ.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||03-10-2000||12:49 PM||||I'm afraid that I must agree with MM. I think it would lead to to a lot of hurt feelings. Do we really want to do that to ourselves? <BR>AOL has chat room hosts (guides?) that can be "paged" when someone gets out of line. Is anyone going to moderate "our" room in real time? Just don't think it's a good idea.<P>Besides...  I would never get *any* work done.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||9
