Z||000015||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||08:18 PM||||Other list members help me out here...<P>I know there is a fiero chat on Wednesday's at 8 p.m. somewhere out there, I just can't remember where.  It has been around for at least 6 mos.  I only checked in once and it was D E  A   D ...  That way though if we all wanted to invade we wouldn't feel like outsiders.<P>While I tend to agree with MM that things have been a little heated lately, I disagree that a chat room would be more or less inclined to heated discussions.  I guess I can't really see why it would be any different from any other chat room.  It might be for Fiero owners, but not be Fiero related.  I think that here we often talk about topics we wouldn't feel appropriate talking about in real time.  Also, it is much easier to apologize in real time.  If I post something offensive to the Forum, I might or might not see the offended's response for several days.  Then also in real time, even if an awful comment is made, it usually scrolls so fast that it is gone before many folks see it.  <P>I would be willing to set up a room on msn chatcity.  If anyone is interested let me know.<P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||6
Z||000016||Ozzy||03-11-2000||12:46 AM||||Hey Guys..<P>I don't see what the problem is.  Cliff, did you ever check out the Ford F150 online chat room I mentioned some time ago???<P>Unless we Fiero owners are 'less' civilised than Ford truck owners (God forbid!) this particular chat room works very well with little, to no problems. Folks are generally respectfull and helpfull. (I also own a '97 F250) The website additionally runs the Ultimate Bulletin Board software or something very similar. They have discounts, deals etc, etc. (Don't mean to plug)<P>Real time chat rooms reveal more of the real personality of the participants. Every one here seems to be very protective and greatfull for Cliff's web site and if some bone head was to come in (as proven recently) I think we could dispose of them in an intelligent manner.<P>I mentioned this quite some time ago and still would absolutley luv to see this. I know Fierodave and some others have started this off elsewhere on the web but every time I go there there is no one in the room. If it was part of this site I think it would be very popular. I think it would be a blast to chat with some of you folks in real time.<P><BR>Here is the Ford site if you are curious.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.f150online.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.f150online.com/</A> <P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000017||Ozzy||03-12-2000||04:05 PM||||I was kinda hoping this would catch some support this time but guess not.<P>I don't mean to nag Cliff. I'm sure there is good reason as to why this isn't an option.<P>Luv the Forum anyway...Has saved me SOOOOOOOOO much time and money. I also know of NO other website that I make a point of hitting every day. I'm very thankfull you don't run those horid advertising banners and such.<P>Thnx,<P>ozzy||||reg||1
